    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34f37bec_c8508665",
        "filename": "arch/arm64/configs/gki_defconfig",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 383,
      "author": {
        "id": 1010110
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-14T01:16:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "On this one, we run into trouble because the display smmu (smmu is built in) uses the gpucc (now a module) as the power domain. As we initialize the power domain via __genpd_dev_pm_attach(), we call driver_deferred_probe_check_state() which after initcall_done is set, returns ENODEV which causes the smmu to fail to initialize, despite the gpucc module loading shortly afterwards.\n\nI\u0027ve dug around and it looks like reverting https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/commit/?id\u003de01afc32502555beb2057ddd74401be38475d851\n\nlets it work when the gpucc is a module.\n\nI\u0027ll need to see what a proper fix would be for this.",
      "parentUuid": "4aecb413_717a410d",
      "revId": "85d424fe79c2a69c895f46196873d4928873239c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
